-- ============================================================
-- Spirit Bond: notes
-- ============================================================
--
-- TODO.md: "Spirit Bond (0, 4): While your pet is active, you and your pet
-- regenerate 2% of total health every 10 sec, ~~and healing done to you and your
-- pet is increased by 10%~~ and Mend Pet is 50/100% more effective. (2 ranks)"
--
-- Entirely DBC.  No script, no spell_proc, no new spell.
--
-- The retail plumbing is already the right shape and is left alone:
-- spell_pet_auras carries (19578,0,0,19579) and (20895,0,0,24529), and both
-- payloads are SPELL_EFFECT_APPLY_AREA_AURA_PET, so the hunter AND the pet get
-- them from one cast.  That is the half the TODO says to keep.
--
-- The 2%/10s regen is already exactly right at rank 2: 24529's Effect1 is
-- OBS_MOD_HEALTH with base points 1 + die sides 1 = 2, amplitude 10000.  (Rank 1
-- is 1%, which is the correct half-step.)  Untouched.
--
-- Removed: Effect2 on BOTH payloads, SPELL_AURA_MOD_HEALING_PCT with MiscValue
-- 127 at +5%/+10%.  Zeroing it on the payload drops the bonus from the hunter
-- and the pet in one place, which is why the edit is there rather than on the
-- talent.
--
-- Added: Effect2 on the TALENT ranks.  In retail this was a SPELL_AURA_DUMMY
-- mirroring the healing number purely so $s2 had something to render; it becomes
-- the Mend Pet amplifier.
--
-- EffectMiscValue 22 is SPELLMOD_DOT, and this is the detail the whole talent
-- turns on.  Mend Pet is SPELL_AURA_PERIODIC_HEAL;
-- AuraEffect::HandlePeriodicHealAurasTick feeds its amount to
-- SpellHealingBonusDone with damagetype == DOT, and Unit.cpp:9688 then picks
-- `damagetype == DOT ? SPELLMOD_DOT : SPELLMOD_DAMAGE`.  MiscValue 0
-- (SPELLMOD_DAMAGE) is the obvious guess and does nothing at all.
--
-- SpellFamilyName is set to 9 on both ranks -- retail left it at 0, and
-- SpellInfo::IsAffectedBySpellMod requires the modifier's family to match the
-- modified spell's, so a class mask on a family-0 aura would never match Mend
-- Pet.  Class mask A 0x800000 is the Mend Pet chain (136/3111/3661/3662/13542/
-- 13543/13544/27046/48989/48990); B and C are explicitly zeroed.
